<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arboga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arboga is a small town in Västmanland in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, a medieval trading centre for the iron of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergslagen">Bergslagen</a> mining district. The meeting held there in 1435 during Engelbrekt's revolt, attended by nobles, clergy, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghers">burghers</a> and peasants, is conventionally regarded as the first Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riksdag">Riksdag</a>, and further national assemblies met there in the following century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arboga.jpg" alt="Arboga" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jssfrk · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arboga_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
